==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|resipiscence}}, or its source, {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|resipiscentia}}, from the present participle of {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|resipiscere|resipīscere|to regain consciousness, come to one's senses}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌɹɛsɪˈpɪsəns/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|_|literary}} [[repentance|Repentance]]; recognition of a past mistake, especially with a desire to improve in the future. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}

